{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>The Hanochite family.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory (Yalkut Shim'oni, Numbers §593) said, and this is their language: Rav Idi said — a heh at the beginning of the words and a yod at their end — Yah testifies concerning them that they are the children of their fathers. And what is the reason? ״שִׁבְטֵי יָהּ עֵדוּת״ and so forth — end quote." "<b>And I saw [fit]</b> to give a reason why the Name was fixed in them out of order — heh at the beginning and yod at the end — prefacing the words of the earlier masters of blessed memory (Tikkunim 10) that the totality of the souls of Israel is the throne of His glory, may He be blessed, which is called the Sanctuary of His holiness and is designated by the name Adonai. And according to what has preceded us from the men of truth (Tur, Shulchan Aruch, Orach Chayim, siman 5), that everyone who utters the mention of the Name from his mouth must intend the letters that are mentioned in his mouth and those concealed in thought — the ones mentioned being the name Adonai, and the ones concealed being the name YHWH — and also intend the interlocking of the letters, which is the sod of ״HaShem in His holy sanctuary״ (Psalms 11:4). Therefore, when the two names interlock, two letters of HaShem — yod, heh — stand together, heh preceding yod. And these are the letters inscribed in the families of the house of Israel — HaChanochi, HaPalui — in which heh precedes yod, these being the letters of the seal of HaShem in His holy sanctuary. And from the two of them the name Yah, alluded to in the verse ״שִׁבְטֵי יָהּ,״ will be built."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:14:43.015425068Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}